    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0026" n="18" xml:id="pg18"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.014 Antarctic/333</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lothian</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-12-27">December 27, 1939</date>.<lb/>[Received January 2,
                        1940.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: In my letter of the 19th
                        December<anchor n="9" xml:id="d19-f1"/> I had the pleasure of expressing to
                    you my personal appreciation of Admiral Byrd’s humane action in relieving the
                    distress which he and the United States Antarctic Expedition found among the
                    inhabitants of Pitcairn Island.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d19-f2"/></p>
                <p>I duly reported the matter to the Foreign Office and I have now been instructed
                    to convey to you the grateful thanks of His Majesty’s Government for the
                    kindness of Admiral Byrd and the United States Antarctic Expedition.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lothian</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="9" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f2" n="10" xml:id="d19-f2-content">
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">North Star</hi> had visited Pitcairn Island on
                    December 14 with the permission of the British Government to take on water.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
